'''Killer Gross Cat''' (殺意のキモネコ, ''Satsui no Kimoneko'', '''Killer Gross Cat''') is a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy introduced in [[Horde of Cats]]. It was added in [[Version 14.2 Update|Version 14.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Killer Gross Cat
|image = E 719.png
|first appearance = [[Horde of Cats]]
|money drop = 300¢ - 1,185¢
}}

==Enemy==
While its stats at 100% are unimpressive, Killer Gross Cat's strength comes from the magnifications it's given in [[Horde of Cats]]. Its stats range from 118,000 health and 7,080 damage in [[Horde of Cats/Bloodthirsty Lv.1~15|Bloodthirsty Lv.6]] to 480,000 health and 28,800 in Bloodthirsty Lv.MAX, enough to instantly destroy a 20+90 [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]]. Its guaranteed knockback effect is not much of a threat, since it has Single Attack and won't do much when a meatshield would simply dismiss them.

==Strategy==
Because of its Single Attack, Killer Gross Cat is more of a nuisance than a serious threat. As long as you're constantly spamming meatshields, Killer Gross Cat won't be able to tear any holes in your defense and thus attack your stack of [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercats]]. If you own it, [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Crystal Li'l Gau Gau]] can make Killer Gross even more of a joke due to its [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback Immunity]] and [[Resistant|Resistance]] to Black.

As for attackers, [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] will shred it, but is vulnerable to the [[Killer Axe Cat Base (Enemy Base)|Killer Axe Base]] because of his slow speed, so [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] may be better choices. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can also deal some chip damage on top of his slow, plus has the range to stay somewhat safe from the [[Killer Axe Cat Base (Enemy Base)|Killer Axe Cat Base]].

